@* Render firewall for the always-mounted pickers: MessageInput re-renders constantly
   (typing indicator, reply bar, upload progress) and without this wrapper every one of
   those renders would re-diff the huge hidden picker subtrees. ShouldRender=false blocks
   exactly those parent cascades; the pickers' own interactions still render normally,
   because Blazor renders from the component that handled the event, not from the root.
   Callers @key this component when the content's SHAPE must change (e.g. the
   mobile↔desktop picker swap) — a new key makes a fresh instance, and a first render
   always happens regardless of ShouldRender. *@
@ChildContent

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    protected override bool ShouldRender() => false;
}
